---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj01.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Treasury Shares (自己株式) — Presentation as a Deduction From Net Assets" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Acquisition and Disposal of Treasury Shares" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Gains/Losses on Disposal — Adjustments to Capital Surplus, Not Profit or Loss" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Legal Reserve (法定準備金) — Capital Reserve and Earned Reserve" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Reduction (Appropriation) of Legal Reserve" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Disposal of Treasury Shares at a Gain" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Negative Other Capital Surplus at Year End" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Treasury shares as a contra-equity item, not an asset — and legal reserves as a Companies Act construct</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 1 addresses TWO related, but distinct, questions arising from Japan's Companies Act (会社法): how should an entity account for TREASURY SHARES (自己株式) — its own shares reacquired and held — and how should movements in LEGAL RESERVES (法定準備金, reserves the Companies Act REQUIRES certain companies to maintain) be recognised. Both concepts sit WITHIN the Net Assets (純資産) section of the Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) rather than affecting profit or loss, reflecting that transactions with a company's OWN shareholders, in their capacity as owners, are NOT income-statement events.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies applying J-GAAP</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies preparing financial statements under Japanese GAAP that ACQUIRE, HOLD, or DISPOSE OF treasury shares, or that maintain (and may need to REDUCE) legal reserves under the Companies Act.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Treasury Shares (自己株式) — Presentation as a Deduction From Net Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Recorded at cost, deducted at the foot of Shareholders' Equity</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Treasury shares are recorded at ACQUISITION COST and presented as a <strong>DEDUCTION</strong> at the FOOT of the Shareholders' Equity (株主資本) subsection, WITHIN the broader Net Assets (純資産) section of the Balance Sheet — they are NEVER recognised as an ASSET, reflecting that a company cannot genuinely "own" a claim against itself.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Acquisition and Disposal of Treasury Shares</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A transaction with owners, in their capacity as owners</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">ACQUIRING treasury shares REDUCES Net Assets by the CONSIDERATION paid (recorded as an increase in the negative treasury shares balance). DISPOSING of treasury shares (e.g. reissuing them) is treated as a further TRANSACTION with shareholders, NOT as a sale of an asset — consistent with the view that Net Assets movements arising from an entity's OWN equity instruments are capital transactions.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Gains/Losses on Disposal — Adjustments to Capital Surplus, Not Profit or Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Never recognised in the Statement of Income</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Where treasury shares are DISPOSED OF at a price DIFFERENT from their recorded cost, the DIFFERENCE is recognised as an adjustment to "OTHER CAPITAL SURPLUS" (その他資本剰余金) — a component of Capital Surplus (資本剰余金) within Shareholders' Equity — and is <strong>NEVER</strong> recognised as a GAIN or LOSS in the Statement of Income (損益計算書, P&amp;L). This reflects the general principle that transactions in an entity's OWN equity instruments do not generate profit or loss, regardless of the price at which they are transacted.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Legal Reserve (法定準備金) — Capital Reserve and Earned Reserve</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A Companies Act-mandated buffer, split into two components</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-2"><span>Legal reserve component</span><span>Description</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2"><span>Capital Reserve (資本準備金)</span><span>A reserve arising from CAPITAL transactions — e.g. the portion of share issuance proceeds NOT credited to Common Stock (資本金) — a component of Capital Surplus</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-2"><span>Earned Reserve (利益準備金)</span><span>A reserve set aside from RETAINED EARNINGS, historically REQUIRED under the Companies Act (a portion of dividends/surplus distributions) until reaching a specified threshold relative to Common Stock — a component of Retained Earnings (利益剰余金)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Both are LEGALLY mandated buffers intended to protect creditors by limiting freely distributable amounts — a distinctive feature of Japanese company law without a precise IFRS/US GAAP parallel of the same statutory character.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Reduction (Appropriation) of Legal Reserve</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Requires specific Companies Act procedures, transferred within Net Assets</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">A REDUCTION of legal reserve (e.g. transferring Capital Reserve to Other Capital Surplus, or Earned Reserve to Other Retained Earnings) generally requires a SHAREHOLDERS' RESOLUTION and, in some circumstances, CREDITOR PROTECTION procedures under the Companies Act. Once properly effected, the reduction is recorded as a RECLASSIFICATION WITHIN Net Assets — moving amounts between the "legal reserve" and "other" components of Capital Surplus or Retained Earnings — WITHOUT any effect on the Statement of Income.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Disposal of Treasury Shares at a Gain</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Crediting Other Capital Surplus, not the Statement of Income</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Reissuing treasury shares above their recorded cost</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds treasury shares recorded at ¥50,000,000 cost, and disposes of them (e.g. to satisfy a stock-based compensation exercise) for ¥62,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The ¥12,000,000 difference (¥62,000,000 − ¥50,000,000) is credited to <strong>Other Capital Surplus</strong> WITHIN Net Assets — NOT recognised as a ¥12,000,000 gain in the Statement of Income, consistent with the principle that transactions in the company's own shares are capital transactions.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Negative Other Capital Surplus at Year End</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A mechanical year-end correction rule</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Repeated treasury share losses driving Other Capital Surplus negative</div><div class="wk-body">Due to several treasury share disposals at a loss during the year, a company's "Other Capital Surplus" balance becomes negative (a debit balance of ¥8,000,000) at the fiscal year end.</div><div class="wk-answer">Under ASBJ Statement No. 1's specific mechanical rule, the NEGATIVE ¥8,000,000 balance is <strong>TRANSFERRED FROM Other Retained Earnings</strong> (その他利益剰余金) at year end, bringing Other Capital Surplus back to zero — a distinctive, PRESCRIPTIVE year-end correction mechanism specific to J-GAAP's Net Assets presentation structure.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 1 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Movements in treasury shares during the period (acquisitions, disposals, cancellations)</span><span>Movements in Capital Reserve and Earned Reserve, including any reductions and the resolutions authorising them</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether Companies Act procedural requirements (shareholder resolution, creditor protection) have been properly satisfied for a legal reserve reduction</span></div></div>
        <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Statement is largely mechanical/procedural in nature</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 1)</span><span>IFRS</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Treasury shares as an asset</span><span>NEVER — deducted from Net Assets</span><span>NEVER — deducted from equity (IAS 32) — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Gain/loss on treasury share transactions</span><span>Adjusts Capital Surplus, never profit or loss</span><span>Adjusts equity directly, never profit or loss (IAS 32) — converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Statutory legal reserve concept</span><span>Capital Reserve / Earned Reserve required under the Companies Act, with specific reduction procedures</span><span>NO equivalent statutory reserve concept under IFRS itself — a matter of LOCAL company law, not IFRS</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">The CORE treasury share accounting principle is genuinely converged with IFRS. The LEGAL RESERVE concept, however, is a distinctly Japanese COMPANIES ACT construct — IFRS has no equivalent, since statutory reserve requirements are a matter of NATIONAL company law everywhere, not an IFRS accounting requirement.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every event under this Statement lands</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Treasury share acquisition/disposal</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Recorded within Net Assets, never through the Statement of Income</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Legal reserve reduction</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Reclassified within Net Assets components</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Presentation of Net Assets in the Balance Sheet — supplies the overall Net Assets structure this Statement's items sit within</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 6</span><span>Statement of Changes in Net Assets — presents the movements this Statement gives rise to</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Treasury shares (自己株式)</div><div class="glossary-def">A company's own shares reacquired and held, recorded at cost and deducted from Shareholders' Equity within Net Assets.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Legal reserve (法定準備金)</div><div class="glossary-def">Companies Act-mandated reserves comprising Capital Reserve (from capital transactions) and Earned Reserve (from retained earnings), protecting creditors by limiting freely distributable amounts.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">Other Capital Surplus (その他資本剰余金)</div><div class="glossary-def">The non-legally-restricted component of Capital Surplus, absorbing gains/losses on treasury share disposals.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
